{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772983938,"nonce":"qpB2l2d1qaecqZ5zdOo2bh49o34=","title":"Implement GitHub Issues tracker adapter","message":"## Summary\n\nImplement the `GitHubIssuesTracker` adapter in `adapters/trackers/github_issues.py`. Currently it's a stub with all methods raising `NotImplementedError`. It needs to fully implement the `IssueTracker` protocol from `core/protocols.py`.\n\n## Requirements\n\n1. **Authentication**: Use GitHub PAT via `GITHUB_TOKEN` env var (already in `.env.example`). Use `requests` (already a dependency) with token in `Authorization` header.\n\n2. **Implement all `IssueTracker` protocol methods**:\n   - `get_issue(issue_id)` — GET `/repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/{number}`, return `TrackerIssue`\n   - `add_comment(issue_id, body)` — POST comment on issue\n   - `list_comments(issue_id)` — GET comments, return list of `TrackerComment`\n   - `set_labels(issue_id, labels)` / `get_labels(issue_id)` — label CRUD\n   - `close_issue(issue_id)` / `open_issue(issue_id)` — status changes via PATCH\n   - `search_issues(query)` — GET `/search/issues` for related-issue search\n   - `sync()` — no-op (GitHub is already remote, unlike git-bug which needs pull/push)\n\n3. **Config integration**: Register in `TRACKER_REGISTRY` in `core/config.py` so `kind: github` works in WORKFLOW.md. Config should accept `repo` (owner/repo) and `token` ($GITHUB_TOKEN).\n\n4. **WORKFLOW.md template**: Update the `init` scaffold to offer a GitHub tracker option or document it in comments.\n\n5. **Error handling**: Raise meaningful errors on 401/403/404. Respect rate limits (check `X-RateLimit-Remaining` header, log warnings when low).\n\n6. **Tests**: Add tests in `tests/adapters/test_github_tracker.py` using mocked HTTP responses (no real API calls in tests).\n\n## Reference\n\n- Protocol definition: `core/protocols.py` — `IssueTracker` protocol\n- Existing adapter for reference: `adapters/trackers/git_bug.py`\n- Registry: `core/config.py` — `TRACKER_REGISTRY`","files":null}]}